# The profile SVGs are build artifacts of scripts/generate.py. The daily CI
# workflow regenerates and commits them, so they collide with locally
# regenerated copies on every pull/rebase.
#
# Your local commit already contains an SVG that matches its own config.json, so
# on a REBASE the right resolution is simply to keep the replayed commit's copy.
# The "keep-local-svg" merge driver does exactly that (cp %B %A) — no
# regeneration, no network, and no dependency on any tracked file, so it even
# resolves the first rebase that introduces it. It relies on pulls being rebases
# (setup-merge-driver.sh sets pull.rebase=true); a plain non-rebase merge would
# invert %A/%B and is not the supported flow.
#
# Register it once per clone with scripts/setup-merge-driver.sh (the driver lives
# in .git/config, which is not tracked).
assets/*.svg merge=keep-local-svg
